165	 * by the garbage collector. Entries with reclaimed keys or values may be removed from the cache on
166	 * each cache modification, on occasional cache accesses, or on calls to {@link Cache#cleanUp}; such
167	 * entries may be counted in {@link Cache#size}, but will never be visible to read or write
168	 * operations.
169	 *
170	 * <p>Certain cache configurations will result in the accrual of periodic maintenance tasks which
171	 * will be performed during write operations, or during occasional read operations in the absence of
172	 * writes. The {@link Cache#cleanUp} method of the returned cache will also perform maintenance, but
173	 * calling it should not be necessary with a high throughput cache. Only caches built with {@link
174	 * #removalListener removalListener}, {@link #expireAfterWrite expireAfterWrite}, {@link
175	 * #expireAfterAccess expireAfterAccess}, {@link #weakKeys weakKeys}, {@link #weakValues
176	 * weakValues}, or {@link #softValues softValues} perform periodic maintenance.
177	 *
178	 * <p>The caches produced by {@code CacheBuilder} are serializable, and the deserialized caches
179	 * retain all the configuration properties of the original cache. Note that the serialized form does
180	 * <i>not</i> include cache contents, but only configuration.
181	 *
182	 * <p>See the Guava User Guide article on <a
183	 * href="https://github.com/google/guava/wiki/CachesExplained">caching</a> for a higher-level
